Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 10 13:53:06 2025 +0100

    Fix libc++ feature macros globally in __config_site
    
    Perfetto's __config_site only undefines negative feature macros
    (e.g., /* #undef _LIBCPP_HAS_NO_THREADS */) but doesn't explicitly
    define the positive forms as 1. This causes conditional guards like
    #if _LIBCPP_HAS_THREADS to evaluate to false (undefined = 0),
    disabling standard library features.
    
    This affects multiple components (abseil-cpp, ICU, protobuf, etc.)
    that rely on these features:
    - _LIBCPP_HAS_LOCALIZATION (IO manipulators, streams)
    - _LIBCPP_HAS_MONOTONIC_CLOCK (std::chrono::steady_clock)
    - _LIBCPP_HAS_WIDE_CHARACTERS (wstring, wstring_view)
    - _LIBCPP_HAS_FILESYSTEM (ifstream, ofstream)
    - _LIBCPP_HAS_THREADS (mutex, thread)
    
    Solution: Add sed commands in debian/rules (Step 4) to insert
    #define statements in buildtools/third_party/libc++/__config_site
    after each corresponding /* #undef */ line.
    
    This global approach (vs per-component BUILD.gn patches) ensures
    all components get correct feature availability.

